{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Correcting or recreating a rejected runtime model leaves it unavailable until the rejection block expires or the daemon restarts."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The JSON PATCH API cannot remove a previously assigned default effort, preventing the operator from restoring the backend default without recreating the model."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An older probe can overwrite newer discovery results after a provider is re-enabled, causing routing to skip a served model."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A persisted runtime model that collides with configuration or references a removed provider prevents the daemon from starting."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Smoke omits a skip line for an explicitly disabled provider, but the evidence does not establish that excluding its checks is incorrect."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The helper decodes the model ID itself, so the tests do not verify native HTTP route decoding even though the reproduced production routing works."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Slow fixture startup can cause a test failure unrelated to cleanup, although the reproduction shows this behavior also existed before the change."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An evaluation of a discovered unserved model can invoke the harness and consume a trial instead of skipping it."},{"id":"C5b","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Running smoke against the live database can record an unreleased migration whose subsequent modification prevents later database opens and deploys."}]}